## Instructions
1. Inspect the CI failure logs above to diagnose the root cause.
2. Fix the broken code or tests in the workspace.
3. Run the local test suite and linters to verify that everything passes cleanly.
4. Commit your changes (or amend the previous commit if appropriate).
5. Push the branch to the remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` or `git push --force-with-lease -u origin HEAD` if amended).
6. When the fix is committed and pushed, write the file `ralph.done` with content `success` at the repository root.
7. If genuinely blocked and unable to resolve the failure, write `ralph.escalate` at the repository root describing the blocker, and stop.
